@@section 1
@@title SQ-MND Potted gossypium loot table rewritten, 2026-11-20 ([miners_delight.md](../miners_delight.md) 6, TODO `licence/cd #4`)
@@date 2026-11-20
@@jars creativedelight
@@sources kubejs/data/miners_delight/loot_tables/blocks/potted_gossypium.json
@@text
@@text Pack data file only (`kubejs/data/miners_delight/`); `/reload` or a plain boot. Any world.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-MND-18 | potted gossypium drops the pot and the gossypium
@group any
@commands place `miners_delight:potted_gossypium`, break it with `/setblock ... air destroy`; count the item entities
@pass one `minecraft:flower_pot` and one `miners_delight:gossypium` drop; no loot table parse error for `miners_delight:blocks/potted_gossypium` in the log
@fails `kubejs/data/miners_delight/loot_tables/blocks/potted_gossypium.json` (one pool, one `minecraft:group` entry with both items; a plain two-entry pool would drop only one of them)
> forceload add -16 -16 16 16
> setblock 4 100 4 minecraft:stone
> setblock 4 101 4 miners_delight:potted_gossypium
> setblock 4 101 4 minecraft:air destroy
sleep 1
> execute if entity @e[type=item,nbt={Item:{id:"minecraft:flower_pot"}},x=4,y=101,z=4,distance=..3]
> execute if entity @e[type=item,nbt={Item:{id:"miners_delight:gossypium"}},x=4,y=101,z=4,distance=..3]
reject Couldn't parse loot table.*potted_gossypium
reject Test failed
look both execute lines "Test passed"
> kill @e[type=item]
